                <pb facs="0182" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Guatemala</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hawks</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-22T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Your 178 [<hi rendition="#italic">118</hi>], October 19, 11 a.m. You may
                    inform the Minister of Foreign Affairs that the Department has been pleased to
                    observe the active efforts of his Government to prevent revolutionary activity
                    on its soil directed against the Honduran Government and if the Guatemalan
                    Government is satisfied that General Jeffries is engaging in revolutionary
                    activities this Department would have no objection to his being deported from
                    Guatemala or placed under police surveillance while in that Republic if the
                    Guatemalan Government believes such action necessary to enable it to comply with
                    its treaty obligations.</p>
                <p>In view of past activities of General Jeffries in Central America you may also
                    inform him personally that he cannot expect to receive the protection of this
                    Government if he participates in any revolutionary activities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
